when Adam Lanza shot his way into Sandy  Hook elementary school he was carrying  three weapons and hundreds of rounds of  ammunition acting alone in just 11  minutes  he used an assault rifle to murder 20  children and six members of staff before  killing himself he was 20 years old and  a former pupil at the school as a  community grieved an America reeled the  question was why but now after a  year-long investigation Connecticut  officials say they may never be able to  answer as they combed through Lanza's  home investigators did find signs of a  disturbed man evidence of target  practice violent computer games in  literature an empty gun cupboard the  rifle he used to kill his mother before  he went to the school computer searches  revealed an obsession with mass murder  particularly the Columbine school  shooting he had made a spreadsheet  listing prerequisites for mass murder  there was a video dramatization of  children being shot and a game called  school shooting despite all of this and  significant mental health issues  investigators said he wasn't aggressive  or threatening before this attack there  were simply no reasonable explanation or  excuse they said for what he did  in the aftermath President Obama tried  and failed to tighten gun laws his  supporters may hope this new report  reignites that debate but Sandy Hook is  gone now and many of the families are  still grieving and they still want  answers Hannah tars Peter Sky News  Newtown Connecticut
 

